Number Chain Rules: 
- Played on a 6x6 board
- Both players start with a chain of numbers from 1 to 3 from their right corner diagnoally to the middle
- Chain off of any of your numbers to unblocked adjacnet sqaures with a number one higher than the number chained from
- Winner is the player with the highest number reached at the end of their chain

Program Description: 
Game is displayed using a bitmap. Players move validated by checked that number chained from is one less than new number and the square is unblocked. 
The Player and the program take turns chaining numbers in unblocked adjacent squares until the board is filled. The winner is the player with the highest number reached.

Challenges Faced: 
Bitmap vs ascii board in console
How to choose where number goes: use just destination or destination and source?
Are positions saved and if so in where: saved in an array? how should you change values?

Decisions Made:
Used a ascii board in the console because bitmap doesn't support numbers inside it so it wouldn't look great.
Used destination and source despite the extra hassel it makes it easier to program and provides the user more control.
Positions are saved in an array. 

